  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Before starting",
      "items": [
        "The device must be enabled and have a recorded original profile with profile-installation rights. The replacement must keep the management endpoint and MDM topic.",
        "The admin action requires replaceEnrollmentProfile authority. Preparation stores the replacement command outside the ordinary command queue.",
        "Preparing the attempt does not send a wake. The operator or bench requests APNs separately. Only the old identity may fetch the credential-bearing InstallProfile; candidate traffic cannot retrieve ordinary queued commands."
      ],
      "dot": "policy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Commit conditions",
      "items": [
        "Promotion requires candidate Authenticate, a valid device-channel TokenUpdate, and acknowledgement of the delivered InstallProfile command. Authenticate must precede TokenUpdate; acknowledgement may arrive before or after those check-ins.",
        "The original top-level profile and MDM payload metadata are retained; the identity payload receives a fresh UUID and issuance authorization. A replacement can select SCEP or ACME.",
        "A candidate user-channel TokenUpdate is staged but does not satisfy the required device-channel token. Promotion is atomic; later stale command results cannot undo it."
      ],
      "dot": "policy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Unsuccessful attempts",
      "items": [
        "Error or CommandFormatError fails the attempt; cancellation and expiry also end it without promoting the candidate. NotNow leaves the attempt pending.",
        "The replacement transition preserves the working enrollment, queue, escrow, DDM state and user channels. An independent CheckOut still disables the enrollment. Server preservation does not establish device-side recovery from every failure.",
        "New issuance is authorized for 30 minutes. Recording a candidate certificate extends the reconciliation deadline to its NotAfter time, if later. Storage checks expiry during transitions, including reads; there is no background expiry worker."
      ],
      "dot": "failure"
    },
    {
      "dot": "neutral",
      "title": "Device acceptance",
      "items": [
        "Verify fresh device and installing-user commands before and after replacement and restart. Test a controlled issuance refusal and confirm that the previous identity remains usable.",
        "Automated state-transition tests establish server preservation. Device-side rollback and acceptance on each OS and enrollment mode require separate live checks."
      ]
    },
    {
